   "text": "## 🧪 Quality review\n\nReviewed against issue #2's acceptance criteria and its 🏛 Design comment, in a fresh worktree\nof `feat/issue-2` (`36941af`).\n\n**Evidence reused, not re-run.** Board here: `npm ci` · `npm run typecheck` · `npm test`\n(86/86) · `npm run lint` · `check-anchors.mjs` → **all exit 0**; anchors report\n`22 D · 16 G · 10 M rows, every reference resolves`. Every `D-`/`G-`/`M-` reference in the diff\nhas a row, the D-016/D-017 addenda sit on the rows they amend, and M-001 labels itself as one\nrun on one machine with a warm npm cache — the honest label, not a median dressed up as one.\n\n**Two mutations of my own** (neither in the PR's table of 18), applied and reverted; tree clean\nafter both:\n\n| Mutation | Result |\n|---|---|\n| delete the `claims.exp <= now` check from `verifyToken` | 🔴 `test/auth/token.test.ts` — expiry is covered, not just the MAC |\n| `org_id = ?` → `? IS NOT NULL` in `auditRepo.listForRequisition` | 🔴 `test/db/tenancy-leak.test.ts` (12 pass, 1 fail) — the harness reaches the audit read path, not only `peopleRepo` |\n\nThe shape holds up where it matters: `Tx` really is unforgeable outside `withTransaction`, every\nrepository statement binds `scope.orgId` first, `instance.ts` is the only unscoped module, the\nappend-only triggers are in the schema as well as in the scan, and `resolveScope` caches nothing.\n\n---\n\n### 🔴 Must fix\n\n**1. `roundHalfUp` returns a non-safe integer for inputs it has just validated as safe —\n`src/domain/money.ts:116`.**\n\n```js\nreturn Math.floor((2 * numerator + denominator) / (2 * denominator));\n```\n\nThe guards above it require both arguments to be safe integers, and then the body forms\n`2 * numerator + denominator` without the ceiling check the rest of the file applies before every\nmultiplication (compare `lineTotal`, `src/domain/money.ts:65`, which divides first precisely to\navoid this). Verified:\n\n```\nroundHalfUp(MAX_SAFE_MINOR, 1) → 9007199254740992   (correct: 9007199254740991)\n```\n\nThe answer is one minor unit too large *and* is outside the safe-integer range the whole money\nmodule is built on — the one arithmetic property this file exists to guarantee. The suite cannot\nsee it: `test/domain/money.test.ts:115` samples `(5,10) (4,10) (15,10) (0,3) (7,1)` and no case\nanywhere near the ceiling, so this is the \"check that cannot produce the case\" pattern the\nstandards name — every other money helper got a ceiling test, this one did not.\n\nIt is unreachable in v1, and the scan at `money.test.ts:126` pins that. But it is exported from\nthe public surface at `src/index.ts:25` as the single rounding function D-003 mandates, so split\n02/03 reaches it the first time a percentage or a split total appears. Fix is two lines:\n\n```ts\nreturn Math.floor(numerator / denominator) + (2 * (numerator % denominator) >= denominator ? 1 : 0);\n```\n\nplus a ceiling case in the money suite.\n\n### 🟡 Nits\n\n1. **`scripts/mint-token.ts` is linted by nothing.** `eslint.config.js:9` ignores\n   `scripts/**/*.ts`, and `tsconfig.build.json` includes `src/` only — there is no `dist/scripts/`\n   (verified). So the 111 lines of the one token issuer are covered by `tsc` alone, while\n   README's \"eslint over the emitted JS\" reads as if everything is covered. One clause in D-019,\n   or a line in G-016.\n2. **Stale number in the PR body:** it states `eslint . -f json` reports 27 entries; here it\n   reports **31** (26 under `dist/`, 4 under `docs/presentation/`, plus `eslint.config.js`). The\n   point — lint is doing work, not passing on an empty set — holds; the figure does not.\n3. **`--ttl` is unbounded** (`scripts/mint-token.ts:60`): any positive safe integer is accepted,\n   so a fat-fingered `--ttl 99999999999` mints a credential good for ~3 000 years. With\n   revocation still open (G-013) that is unrecoverable short of rotating the org secret. A cap\n   (90 days?) is a two-line refusal.\n4. **The log redaction is one level deep** (`src/log.ts:27`). Verified:\n   `log('info','x',{token:'…',ctx:{token:'SECRET2'}})` prints\n   `\"token\":\"[redacted]\",\"ctx\":{\"token\":\"SECRET2\"}`. Nothing logs a nested object today, so this\n   is latent — but D-018's \"tokens … are redacted by the one log function\" is written wider than\n   the code, and #3 is the split that will start logging request context.\n5. **`Object.freeze` is shallow** (`src/config.ts:83`): `tokenKeys` is a real `Map` behind a\n   `ReadonlyMap` type, so the \"frozen typed config\" of D-018 stops at the top level. TypeScript\n   catches the mutation; JavaScript at the `dist/` boundary does not.\n\nOn the **size deviation**: the arithmetic in the PR body is right — cutting at the auth seam\nleaves PR-A above the ceiling anyway — and splitting now buys a second review round on a\n`risk:high` task while #3/#4/#5 wait. I would not cut it. The overrun is already logged for M-009.\n\nVERDICT: findings (1 red, 5 nits)\n",
