   "text": "## 🔧 Fix round 1 — commit `9e29d6b`\n\nBoard from this worktree, every step exit 0:\n`npm ci && npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run lint && check-anchors && render --check`\n→ **99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail** (86 before), anchors `22 D · 16 G · 10 M, every reference\nresolves`, render `19 generated files match`. Seven mutations applied and reverted, all seven\nred; the table is in the PR body under *Fix round 1*.\n\n| Finding | What I did |\n|---|---|\n| 🧪 🔴 1 · `roundHalfUp` leaves the safe-integer range | **Fixed** — divides first, decides the half on the remainder (`src/domain/money.ts:116`). Ceiling cases added: `(MAX_SAFE_MINOR,1)`, `(MAX_SAFE_MINOR,2)` = 4 503 599 627 370 496, `(MAX_SAFE_MINOR-1,2)`, `(MAX_SAFE_MINOR, MAX_SAFE_MINOR)`, plus `Number.isSafeInteger` on the result. Restoring the old expression → 🔴 `test/domain/money` (9/1). |\n| 🔐 🟡 1 · malleable signature encoding | **Fixed** — `signatureB64 === expected.toString('base64url')` after the `timingSafeEqual`. The test *derives* the malleable spellings from the alphabet and asserts there are exactly 3, so if the encoding ever stops being malleable the case fails loudly instead of passing empty. Dropping the line → 🔴 `test/auth/token` (14/1). |\n| 🔐 🟡 2 · `writeAudit` does not scope its foreign references | **Fixed** — `writeAudit` now returns `Result<AuditLine>` and refuses `not_found` when `requisitionId` or `actorPersonId` is not in the scope's organisation. Test: B writes about A's requisition and credits A's person → two refusals, `audit.list` for B is still 0, then B's own references are accepted and the count is 1. Dropping both guards → 🔴 `test/db/tenancy-leak` (19/1). |\n| 🔐 🟡 3 · the leak table covers repositories, not methods | **Fixed** — 4 read cases (`people.list`, `catalogue.list`, `audit.list`, `requisitions.list({buyerPersonId})`) and 3 write cases (cross-org buyer, cross-org catalogue item, the audit reference above). `people.list` asserts the sharper thing — B's list does not *contain* A's person — because B legitimately has people of its own. Table presence guard raised 9 → 13. |\n| 🔐 🟡 4 / 🧪 🟡 4 · redaction | **Fixed together** — `redact` walks the whole tree (objects and arrays, depth-capped at 6, which also makes a cyclic field safe), the key list gains `bearer`, `auth_?header` and `credential`, and any *value* matching `^v\\d+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$` is redacted whatever its field is called. Top-level-only → 🔴 `test/config/log` (1/2). |\n| 🧪 🟡 1 · `scripts/**` is linted by nothing | **Fixed** — new `tsconfig.lint.json` emits `src/` + `scripts/` into the gitignored `dist-lint/`; `npm run lint` runs it and eslint lints `dist-lint/scripts/**/*.js` (`dist-lint/src/` is ignored, it is the same code as `dist/`). `==` in `scripts/mint-token.ts` → 🔴 `npm run lint`. D-019 addendum + a note on G-016; README's lint line corrected. |\n| 🧪 🟡 2 · stale eslint count | **Fixed** — the body now says **32 entries** (26 `dist/`, 1 `dist-lint/scripts/`, 4 `docs/presentation/`, `eslint.config.js`) and says the old figure was wrong. |\n| 🧪 🟡 3 · `--ttl` unbounded | **Fixed** — `MAX_TTL_SECONDS = 90 * 86 400`, a refusal above it, with a test at the cap (mints) and one above it (exit 1, no token). |\n| 🧪 🟡 5 · `Object.freeze` is shallow | **Fixed** — `tokenKeys` is handed out as a frozen read-only view with no `set`/`delete`/`clear`; the test checks the mutators are gone, that assigning over `get` throws, and that reads and iteration still work. Handing out the raw `Map` → 🔴 `test/config/startup` (6/1). |\n| 🔐 note / 🧪 note · the size deviation | **Not a code change**, as both reviews said. The quality review's conclusion stands (cutting now buys a review round while #3/#4/#5 wait); the overrun stays logged for M-009 and is FRZWLF's call. |\n\nNothing declined. The two reviews' 🔴 and all 9 🟡 are addressed in code or in the body.\n",
