   "text": "## 🧪 Quality review — re-review after fix round 1 (`9e29d6b`)\n\nScope: new 🔴 only, per the fix-round rule. Evidence reused from the fixer's report (seven\nmutations, the anchor and render checks); here I re-ran `npm ci && npm test` once →\n**99 tests, 99 pass, 0 fail, exit 0** (86 before), and `npm run typecheck` → exit 0.\n\n**The 🔴 is correctly fixed.** `src/domain/money.ts:113-120` now divides first and decides the\nhalf on the remainder. I checked the new expression against exact `BigInt` arithmetic rather\nthan against the suite: the two intermediates the old body could not keep safe are both exact\nhere — `numerator % denominator` is exact for safe integers, and `2 * (numerator % denominator)`\nis an even value below 2^54, so it is representable exactly even when `denominator` is near the\nceiling. `Math.floor(numerator / denominator)` was the one place a float division could round a\nquotient up across an integer, so I searched for that: all near-ceiling quotients\n`k*d-1, k*d-2, k*d` for every `d < 200 000`, plus 3 000 000 random safe-integer pairs — **no\nmismatch against `BigInt`**, and `roundHalfUp(MAX_SAFE_MINOR, 1)` now returns `9007199254740991`.\nThe `numerator < 0` guard makes the `%`/`Math.floor` sign asymmetry unreachable, so the\n\"away from zero\" wording in the test name stays true for the accepted domain.\n\n**My mutation** (`>=` → `>` on the half decision, applied and reverted; tree clean after):\n🔴 `test/domain/money.test.ts` (97/2) — the new ceiling cases really do pin the half, not just\nthe magnitude. The suite can now produce the case it could not before.\n\n**Nits checked off the fixer's report**, not re-opened: 🟡 1 `scripts/**` is emitted through\n`tsconfig.lint.json` into `dist-lint/` and linted (`eslint.config.js`, `package.json`) · 🟡 2 the\nbody's eslint figure is corrected to 32 and says the old one was wrong · 🟡 3 `--ttl` capped at\n90 days with a test at and above the cap · 🟡 4 `redact` walks the tree · 🟡 5 `tokenKeys` is a\nfrozen read-only view. Docs addenda on D-007, D-018, D-019, D-021 and the G-016 note are on the\nrows they amend.\n\nOne thing I looked at because the fix changed a signature and not only a body: `writeAudit` now\nreturns `Result<AuditLine>`. `typecheck` is clean and the only call sites in the tree are in\n`test/`, so no caller silently drops a refusal today. Worth a `must(...)` at the first `src/`\ncall site in split 02 — that is a note for the implementer, not a finding.\n\nNo new 🔴. The size deviation stays FRZWLF's call, as both reviews said.\n\nVERDICT: clean\n",
